# Source Layer

## Data Sources

The data warehouse ingests data from multiple business systems.

| Source | Object Type | Interface |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| CRM | CSV Files | Files in Folder |
| ERP | CSV Files | Files in Folder |

---

# Bronze Layer

## Purpose

Stores raw data exactly as received from source systems.

### Object Type

- Table

### Load Strategy

- Batch Processing
- Full Load
- Truncate & Insert

### Transformations

- None

### Data Model

- None (As-Is)

---

# Silver Layer

## Purpose

Stores cleaned and standardized data.

### Object Type

- Table

### Load Strategy

- Batch Processing
- Full Load
- Truncate & Insert

### Transformations

- Data Cleaning
- Data Standardization
- Data Normalization
- Derived Columns
- Data Enrichment

### Data Model

- None (As-Is)

---

# Gold Layer

## Purpose

Stores business-ready datasets optimized for reporting and analytics.

### Object Type

- Views

### Load Strategy

- No Load

### Transformations

- Data Integration
- Aggregations
- Business Logic

### Data Model

- Star Schema
- Fact Tables
- Aggregate Tables

---

# Consumption Layer

The Gold Layer serves multiple business use cases.

| Consumer | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| 📊 BI & Reporting | Interactive dashboards and business reporting |
| 🔍 Ad-Hoc SQL Queries | Business analysis using SQL |
| 🤖 Machine Learning | Predictive analytics and AI models |

